WERK changes to vendored code (2026): remove scalar_type.hpp's libtorch exception dependency;
extend Marlin FP4 type validation to exact 16-bit block scales; add GPU-resident expert
row bounds and remainder handling; write reduced FP32 accumulators directly into GGML
outputs before the normal model global-scale operation. Unmodified FP4 dequantization
and BF16 tensor-core MMA from Marlin remain in use.

New WERK adapter code is covered by the repository's Elastic License 2.0. It implements
GGUF NVFP4 layout conversion, BF16 activation conversion, GGML dense/MoE dispatch,
architecture gates, probe and regression tests. No vLLM inference runtime is included.
